    "detail": "`ciSignature` takes the first log line matching `/timed out after|##\\[error\\]|\\b(?:error|fail(?:ed|ure)?)\\b/i`. Passing test names containing 'error' or 'fail', and action inputs such as `continue-on-error: false` or `fail-on-cache-miss`, match before the actual failure. Lines also keep durations such as `[5000.01ms]`, so the same failure produces a different signature on every run. The ledger's \"failing test or error line\" is then wrong, unrelated failures in one job collapse into one signature (the cap is over-applied, and needs_fix items are deduplicated away), and identical failures never aggregate across runs."
